From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Dmitry Afonchenko <undermove1@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 30 Oct 2026 16:27:29 +0400
Subject: [PATCH 59/77] Meridian: Arc's space switching, settings toolbar, back
 arrow over the page
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

- A two-finger swipe on the sidebar drags between spaces: the page follows
  the fingers, the neighbour slides in beside it and the window colour
  blends; past a third it completes, otherwise it springs back. Space dots,
  ⌃1–9 and ⌃⇥ switch with the same slide.
- Settings has Arc's toolbar: the open tab's name on top and a row of tabs
  (icon over label), the first one the member's name with the card and Get
  started.
- The back/forward swipe arrow comes in at the edge of the active page, not
  of the window over the sidebar.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01SwxrQ2eLfJ2bv8cCoG2va1
